<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="045" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Concurrency-safe tracking numbers {invoice}.{n}</title>
    <phase>2 Submission and extraction (WP2)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Concurrency guarantee (two parallel submissions never share a number) enforced against a Dataverse alternate key; a wrong retry rule double-creates or loses rows.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Narrow component with an in-repo reference (RecordCreationService.CreateNumberedAsync) — needs care, not architecture.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>P2-B</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>029</deps>
    <tags>bff, dataverse, concurrency</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add a tracking-number allocator that writes a submission's tracking number {firm invoice number}.{n} (n = 1 for the first submission of that firm invoice number, then 2, 3 …) so that two parallel submissions for the same firm and firm invoice number never share a number, using the alternate key from task 020 and a bounded retry on the duplicate-key fault (FR-10, D-37).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Dataverse alternate keys, optimistic concurrency and xUnit concurrency tests. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>ITrackingNumberAllocator in Services/Finance assigns sprk_trackingnumber and sprk_submissionsequence on an existing sprk_invoicesubmission row (or on create, per the chosen design), retrying on the alternate-key duplicate up to a fixed bound and then failing with a stable code; unit tests cover the retry rule and a dev concurrency test proves uniqueness under parallel allocation.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>FR-10 acceptance: second submission of INV-002 gets INV-002.2; numbering is concurrency-safe. Task 020 creates alternate key sprk_invoicesubmission_firm_trackingnumber on (sprk_vendororg, sprk_trackingnumber) plus sprk_firminvoicenumber and sprk_submissionsequence. Callers: 044 (firm invoice number known at intake) and 049 (number known only after extraction). Resubmission after Return to Firm keeps the firm invoice number and gets the next n (D-37, D-43; linkage is 104's). The brief points at DataverseRegistryConcurrencyStore: it lives in the provisioning control plane (src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Concurrency/DataverseRegistryConcurrencyStore.cs, If-Match row guard) and is not referenced by the BFF; the closer in-BFF pattern is RecordCreationService.CreateNumberedAsync.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Submission/TrackingNumberAllocator.cs (+ ITrackingNumberAllocator)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/FinanceModule.cs (shared append point: one registration)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/RecordCreationService.cs:287 (MaxNumberAttempts) and :527 (CreateNumberedAsync — retry only the alternate-key duplicate; every other fault propagates on the first attempt)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs:3211 (public static IsAlternateKeyDuplicate)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ContactIdentityStore.cs:629-635 (Web API body classification of 0x80060892, if the Web API path is used)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Finance/Submission/TrackingNumberAllocatorTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="029" status="required">sprk_invoicesubmission with the (sprk_vendororg, sprk_trackingnumber) alternate key Active in dev.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Every change under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api follows .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-37">Format exactly {firm invoice number}.{n}: firm invoice number trimmed as submitted, n a positive integer without padding. Sequence is per (firm, firm invoice number) — never global, never across firms.</constraint>
    <constraint source="concurrency">Uniqueness comes from the alternate key, not from a read-then-write check. Next n = 1 + highest sprk_submissionsequence for that firm and firm invoice number (read), then write; on IsAlternateKeyDuplicate re-read and retry; at most 10 attempts (raised from 5 by the owner, D-87: k parallel callers need at most k attempts, and the ten-way case must all get a number), then fail with stable code ebilling.tracking.unavailable. Any other fault propagates on the first attempt (a timeout may have written the row).</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-87 (owner, 2026-10-16)">The tracking number is assigned when the submission is first saved, so it is never blank: the allocator CREATES the sprk_invoicesubmission row with {firm invoice number}.{n} already set (sprk_trackingnumber stays SystemRequired: no placeholder, no schema change). There is no update path. A redelivered create is idempotent by the caller's submission id (the new row's id). D-88: the allocator never refuses because a firm invoice number was seen before.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">The allocator is the only writer of sprk_trackingnumber and sprk_submissionsequence.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Logs carry submission id, attempt count and outcome — the firm invoice number is business data, log it only at Debug.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Dataverse alternate keys and retry</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/data.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/dataverse/entity-operations.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Alternate-key retry" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/RecordCreationService.cs">CreateNumberedAsync: loop with an attempt bound, catch only IsAlternateKeyDuplicate, return null / refusal when exhausted.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context and rigor">Declare rigor FULL. Confirm in dev metadata that the key is (sprk_vendororg, sprk_trackingnumber) and Active.</step>
    <step order="1">Choose the write shape: allocate on create (044 path, number known) and allocate by update (049 path, number known later). Both go through the same allocator method; an update that hits the key duplicate is equally safe to retry (the row is not changed when Dataverse refuses).</step>
    <step order="2">Implement AllocateAsync(submissionId or pending entity, firmId, firmInvoiceNumber) returning the tracking number and n, or a refusal with ebilling.tracking.unavailable.</step>
    <step order="3">Unit tests with a mocked entity service: first submission → .1; existing .1 and .2 → .3; duplicate on first try then success → next n; five duplicates → refusal; a non-duplicate fault → propagates without retry; different firm with the same invoice number → .1.</step>
    <step order="4">Dev concurrency test (integration, Skipped when no Dataverse env is configured): 10 parallel allocations for the same firm and firm invoice number produce 10 distinct numbers; delete the test rows afterwards.</step>
    <step order="5">Build, test, publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`.</step>
    <step order="7">Record deviations and the dev concurrency evidence in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the alternate key in dev is on sprk_trackingnumber alone, or is missing, STOP: allocation is not firm-scoped and two firms sending INV-002 would collide.</trigger>
    <trigger>If parallel allocation in dev produces a duplicate number or more than occasional exhaustion at 10-way concurrency, STOP and present the evidence before raising the bound.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>RecordCreationService.CreateNumberedAsync numbers matters / projects via platform autonumber + alternate key; DataverseRegistryConcurrencyStore is a provisioning-service row guard. Neither produces a per-(firm, invoice number) sequence.</existing>
    <extension>Autonumber cannot produce a sequence scoped per firm and firm invoice number, so CreateNumberedAsync cannot be reused as-is; its retry rule and IsAlternateKeyDuplicate are reused unchanged.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>FR-10 fails: resubmissions cannot get {invoice}.{n}, and parallel month-end submissions (NFR-07) could share a tracking number.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ ; dotnet test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">Services/Finance/Submission/TrackingNumberAllocator.cs, ITrackingNumberAllocator, FinanceModule.cs registration</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/data-mutation/FinanceSubmission/TrackingNumberAllocatorTests.cs (ADR-038 KEEP path; compiled into Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests) and TrackingNumberAllocatorLiveTests.cs (the dev concurrency and redelivery tests)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">First submission of INV-002 for a firm gets INV-002.1; the second gets INV-002.2 (FR-10).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The same firm invoice number under a different firm starts at .1.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A duplicate-key fault triggers a re-read and retry; after the attempt bound the allocator returns ebilling.tracking.unavailable and writes nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a fault that is not an alternate-key duplicate propagates on the first attempt with no retry.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">In dev, 10 parallel allocations for one firm and invoice number yield 10 distinct tracking numbers (evidence in notes); the test reports Skipped when no Dataverse env is configured.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size delta of Sprk.Bff.Api measured against a fresh master build and recorded in task notes; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; dotnet test exits 0.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-10, D-37, D-43, NFR-07. Shared append point: FinanceModule.cs (one registration — re-read before editing). Tracking number may be allocated after extraction when the SPA user did not type a firm invoice number (044 returns null; 049 allocates) - SUPERSEDED by D-87: the number is set at create, 044 creates through the allocator and 049 never allocates. Done 2026-10-16; details, live evidence and the owner decisions in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/045-tracking-number-allocator.md. rework: fix-round-1 task 045</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load every file in knowledge/files before Step 1. Follow task-execute for rigor, checkpoints and quality gates.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
